<description>
Rotate the red segment one quarter-turn clockwise around the grey marker, recoloring its original cells green.

Input structure:
- The grid has a dominant background, exactly one grey marker, and one red
  4-connected segment.
- The red segment is a straight horizontal or vertical bar attached to the
  grey marker at exactly one end.
- The clockwise-rotated red segment fits on the same canvas.

Rule:
- Locate the grey marker and the adjacent red cell, which gives the bar's
  direction away from the marker.
- Recolor every input red cell green.
- Draw a red segment of the same length from the marker in the direction
  obtained by rotating the original direction clockwise.

Key insight:
- The grey marker is the pivot, and the side occupied by the red bar tells
  which perpendicular side receives the new red bar.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "straight red bar attached to a single grey pivot on a dominant background",
  "transform": "recolor the original red bar green; from the grey pivot paint an equal-length red bar in the direction 90 degrees clockwise from the original bar"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-11 rows x 3-11 cols, background BLACK
  colors_in: exactly BLACK, RED, GREY
  pivot:
    count: exactly 1 GREY cell
    placement: must have space >= bar_len in both the bar direction and the CW-rotated direction
  bar:
    color: RED, 4-connected, straight horizontal or vertical
    length: 1-4 cells
    attachment: one end adjacent (4-conn) to the pivot; extends away from pivot
    constraint: rotated destination cells must all be BLACK (no overlap with bar)
  transform:
    - recolor all RED cells to GREEN
    - from pivot, paint equal-length RED bar in CW-rotated direction (up->right, right->down, down->left, left->up)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple enough to build forward)
  steps:
    1. pick grid H in [3,11], W in [3,11]
    2. pick bar_len in [1,4]
    3. pick one of 4 cardinal directions for bar
    4. compute CW-rotated direction
    5. place pivot so bar_len cells fit in both original and rotated directions from pivot, and rotated cells do not overlap bar cells
    6. fill grid BLACK, place GREY pivot, paint RED bar of bar_len extending from pivot in chosen direction
```
